  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe upper level ridge is flattening out today with flow aloft \nbecoming zonal and low and mid level flow becoming \nsouthwesterly. A warm front is lifting into the area tonight, \nwith a few light rain showers possible along it, mainly across \nwestern NY into the Finger Lakes region. Temperatures at 850 mb \nwarms to around 15C to 18C which will support well above average\ntemperatures. Due to the warm air advection with deeper \nmoisture moving in, clouds will limit how warm it could get \nThursday but if we can get a few hours of sun, then a few \npockets of 80 degrees is possible, mainly in NEPA or along the \nNY Thruway corridor. Friday will have a front dropping in from \nthe NW with showers spreading in. NEPA may see more sun ahead of\nthe front with rain not arriving till late afternoon or early \nevening. There is not much instability in place despite the late\nseason warmth, and there is not a lot of forcing along the \nfront so thunderstorms look unlikely Friday but a rumble of \nthunder cant be completely ruled out. The speed of the front and\nlighter stratiform precipitation, rainfall amounts are expected\nto be a half inch or less so flooding and flash flooding is not\na concern. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nThis weekend into early next week, a long wave trough tries to \nset up in the Northeast US. There is a couple chances of 850 mb \ntemps falling below 0C early next week. There is also good \nchances of a strong surface high being in place as well so the \nfirst widespread frost/freeze is possible if skies can remain \nclear Monday night and especially Tuesday night.",
